dsh-screen-use
==============

MIT License (see the SPDX-style grant below).

The native Win32/GDI helpers in `src/` (`win32.cjs`, `capture.cjs`,
`png.cjs`) and the module-resolution helper in `lib/loader.cjs` are adapted
from the MIT-licensed project:

  dsh-computer-use — https://github.com/EvangeliMo/dsh-computer-use
  Copyright (c) the dsh-computer-use contributors

Changes in this package: error prefixes renamed to dsh-screen-use, an
`GetAsyncKeyState` binding plus `escapeDown` / `anyMouseButtonDown` probes
added for the Escape kill switch and takeover detection, and the files were
otherwise left structurally intact so their documented coordinate-space and
PNG-encoding invariants still hold.

Everything else — the shared-pointer runtime, the gates, the token policy, the
tools, the prompt section, the HTTP face and the floating panel — is original
work for dsh-screen-use.

